WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.952
Raj: We'll batch the deletes from now. The large transaction caused the WAL burst.
之后把删除拆成批次，大事务造成这次WAL突增。

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:13.464
Hannah: Disk waits fell after scan throttling. Replay accelerated with the same incoming rate.
扫描降速后磁盘等待下降，在相同日志输入速率下回放加快。

3
00:00:13.464 --> 00:00:19.729
Anika: That supports disk competition as a contributor. It doesn't blame the scan alone.
这支持磁盘竞争是一个促成因素，不是把责任全归扫描。

4
00:00:19.729 --> 00:00:25.993
Priya: So, who's picking this up tomorrow? Raj owns batch sizing tests, right?
那明天谁接？Raj负责批次大小测试，对吧？

5
00:00:25.993 --> 00:00:32.665
Lukas: I'll own scan isolation options Friday. Moving it elsewhere has capacity costs.
我周五负责扫描隔离方案，迁到别处也有容量成本。

6
00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:39.385
Raj: Yes, my action item includes pacing. Maybe row count alone isn't enough.
是，我的行动项也包括批次节奏，可能只限制行数还不够。

7
00:00:39.385 --> 00:00:48.097
Hannah: Measure WAL volume and replay bottleneck together. Test overlaps in an isolated environment.
同时测WAL量和回放瓶颈，在隔离环境测试负载重叠。

8
00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:54.794
Anika: I'll test freshness-aware routing by Friday. Sensitive reads remain on primary meanwhile.
我周五前测试感知新鲜度的路由，期间敏感读仍走主库。

9
00:00:54.794 --> 00:01:02.162
Lukas: Keep failover policy separate from lag routing. Promotion requires durability and fencing checks.
故障切主策略与延迟读路由分开，提升副本需要持久性和隔离旧主检查。

10
00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:08.330
Priya: Okay, close the loop next week. Bring overlap tests and routing evidence.
好，下周闭环，带上重叠负载测试和路由证据。

